<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42074" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rustĭcātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A living in the country</i>, <i>country life</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">neque militia solum, sed etiam peregrinationes
					rusticationesque communes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Lael. 27, 103</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Agriculture</i>, <i>husbandry</i>,
			Col. praef. § 13; 1, 1, 6; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">11, 1, 6: creata ab Altissimo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ecclus. 7, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
